      "rev_n_7_3db1c1_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_3db1c1_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_3db1c1",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through the input precincts once to aggregate vote counts (A and B) for each district into a dictionary or list of objects. Then, loop from district 1 to D to determine the winner, calculate wasted votes based on the specific rules (all losing votes + excess winning votes), print the results immediately, and simultaneously accumulate the global totals for V, wA, and wB. Finally, compute and print the efficiency gap using the accumulated global totals.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8301949402979478773",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794508557.139608
      },
      "rev_n_8_079597_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_079597_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_079597",
        "thought_text": "Use a two-pass approach over the data structure. First pass: read all precinct data and store it grouped by district ID. Second pass: for each district index from 1 to D, retrieve the aggregated votes, calculate the winner and wasted votes, print them, and add to running global sums. After the loop, calculate the final efficiency gap. This ensures the printed per-district values are strictly derived from the district's own data, avoiding the previous logic error where global accumulation interfered with local printing.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8301949402979478773",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794508557.1396286
      },
      "rev_n_9_95919f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_95919f_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_95919f",
        "thought_text": "Implement the solution by defining a helper function to calculate wasted votes given total votes for A and B. Read the input, group precincts by district. Then, for each district, call the helper, print the output, and update global counters. This modularizes the wasted vote logic and clearly separates the per-district reporting from the final efficiency gap calculation, ensuring data integrity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8301949402979478773",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
